<title>USA: Checkmate Electronics wins $1.2 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Checkmate Electronics wins $1.2 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>ROSWELL, Ga. 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Checkmate Electronics Inc said Wednesday it had sold $1.2 million of its check transaction processing equipment to Burlington Coat Factory Warehouse Corp.</p>
<p>Checkmate said Burlington Coat had purchased its CM2020 signature capture and CM2001 debit terminals for their more than 250 stores nationwide, including subsidiaries.</p>
<p>With the purchase, Burlington Coat Factory now has the complete Checkmate Payment System2000.  It had already purchased and installed the Checkmate check readers.</p>
<p>((-- E. Auchard, New York newsdesk, 212-859-1736))</p>
